{"name":"Winner’s Circle","hex":"#365771","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"winner","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who has won or often wins.","A point or goal that wins a competition."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winner"},{"term":"circle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A two-dimensional geometric figure, a line, consisting of the set of all those points in a plane that are equally distant from a given point (center).","A two-dimensional geometric figure, a disk, consisting of the set of all those points of a plane at a distance less than or equal to a fixed distance (radius) from a given point."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To travel around along a curved path; to orbit.","To surround; to encompass within a circle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Circle","blocks":[{"text":"A circle is a shape consisting of all points in a plane that are at a given distance from a given point, the centre. The distance between any point of the circle and the centre is called the radius. The length of a line segment connecting two points on the circle and passing through the centre is called the diameter. A circle bounds a region of the plane called a disc."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Circle-withsegments.svg/330px-Circle-withsegments.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/2009_07_09_camino_cielo_paradise_137.jpg/500px-2009_07_09_camino_cielo_paradise_137.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/2009_07_09_camino_cielo_paradise_137.jpg/1280px-2009_07_09_camino_cielo_paradise_137.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"